Targets: native
Subject: One-file server: embed share/, initdb and the container entrypoint in postgres
Purpose: A FROM scratch image should hold one file. This links everything the server needs besides itself into the postgres executable: the share/ tree as a tar image (file system calls on paths below the share and pkglib directories are answered from it, via ld --wrap), initdb, pg_resetwal and pg_controldata as in-process programs (postgres --initdb, --resetwal, --controldata), the container entrypoint (postgres --launcher: initialise PGDATA on the first start, refuse a directory that is not a cluster, then continue as the server) and a synthesized passwd entry for a user id that /etc/passwd does not know. Everything is behind PG_EMBEDDED_IMAGE and needs the objects the build adds (the tar image, the renamed program mains), so without them the code is upstream's.
Components: src/backend/main/embedded.c (new), src/backend/main/main.c, src/backend/main/Makefile
Checks: scripts/native-image.sh test (cold init, SQL, restart, bad PGDATA) on an image whose only file is /usr/local/pgsql/bin/postgres; scripts/native-image.sh manifest
Origin: own


